

[38;5;231m⏺[39m I'm using the brainstorming skill, and this classifies as [1marchitectural[0m — a notifications system is a new subsystem
  (subscriptions, change events, delivery), not a change to a flow that already exists here. So: questions first, then
  approaches, then a design and a written spec. No code until you approve a design.

  One thing I have to flag before asking anything detailed, because it changes the whole shape of the answer:

  [1mThis repo is an empty static page.[0m The entire codebase is [38;5;153mindex.html[39m — an [38;5;153m<h1>Tasks</h1>[39m and an empty [38;5;153m<main>[39m. There is
  no task model, no users, no persistence, no server, no build tooling. A notification is a message about [3ma change to a[0m
  [3mthing someone has a relationship with[0m, so it needs all four of those to exist: identity (who), tasks with a change
  history (what changed), a subscription concept ("care about"), and a delivery channel. Right now none of them do.

  That means "build a notifications system for this app" is almost certainly not one spec — it's a dependency chain, and
  notifications are at the far end of it. I don't want to spend questions refining digest windows and email templates
  if what you actually need first is tasks and users.

